Dear David,

I am running four half-height disks in my PWS, but not constantly nor
in an overheated room.  When I was learning my way around the machine,
I messed things up pretty badly by adding a new disk at ID 1 (which I
had previously not used)  It knocked everything for a loop.  I had 5.1
at the time.  The 5.x Tru64 doesn't tie the OS device file to the SCSI
ID number.  Rather, the OS assigns a new "dsk" number to each disk
when it is added, and that device keeps that number throughout its
life.

You might want to look into the cloning function to see if it will
work for you in this case; it is also possible to migrate partitions
under Tru64. Dr. Blinn on the Tru64 managers' list would probably give
you and answer quick.  Otherwise, you should be able to do a new
install to a partition on the 18G disk, with separate partitions for
/home and /usr/local, which you would then copy over.  It might take a
bit of owrk to get your new OS installation to recognize all the bits
and pieces in your old /home and /usr partitions, which would still
refer to the old "dsk" device numbers.

